{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat qrypt-quickstart/AGENTS.md qrypt-quickstart/Makefile qrypt-quickstart/mock/run_cases.sh qrypt-quickstart/agent-sandbox/verify.sh'","aggregated_output":"# Guidance for AI coding agents\n\nThis repository has two onboarding modes. Prefer **Quick Setup** unless the human asks for Isolated Setup.\n\nHumans should paste only a short request plus links to the quickstart and `llms.txt`.\nAll rules below (and in `llms.txt`) apply even when the paste-prompt does not repeat them.\n\n## Quick Setup (default, no Docker)\n1. Read https://qrypt-quickstart.pages.dev/llms.txt and the quickstart page.\n2. Pick Python or Node; use the official snippets in `quickstart/`.\n3. Install deps; run mocked tests (`make check` in this repo, or point `QRYPT_BASE_URL` at `mock/server.py`).\n4. Ask the human to create `.env` with `QRYPT_API_KEY` themselves. Never ask them to paste the token into chat, prompts, CLI args or source.\n5. Never read, print or dump `.env` or environment variables. Never enable verbose HTTP logging of Authorization headers.\n6. After the human confirms `.env` is set, run the example. Keep the key in memory only.\n7. Report the success line only. Remind the human to review the session for credential exposure and to rotate any exposed or potentially compromised credentials (including unrelated ones).\n\nThese rules are behavioral safeguards. They do **not** stop an unrestricted agent from reading files. Disposable tokens and Isolated Setup exist for that.\n\n## Isolated Setup (Docker)\n- Human runs `agent-sandbox/run.sh <clean-project> <agent-command>`. The project must not contain `.env`.\n- You (the agent) have no `QRYPT_API_KEY`. Implement and mock-test only.\n- Human runs `agent-sandbox/verify.sh --env <secret-path>` on the host. That runs **fixed** snippets from this repo, not your code, with the real token. Output is sanitized PASS/FAIL.\n- Do not ask for the token. Do not try to read secrets from the host.\n\n## Manual developer path\nHumans who are not using an agent should follow the numbered steps on the quickstart page (token → `.env` → snippet → run). `make check` needs no token.\n# Quickstart: `make check` (no token needed, ~1 min), then optionally `make live-py` or `make live-js` (1 KiB of real entropy each).\n.PHONY: check deps test isolation live-py live-js\ndeps:            ## install Python deps (Node needs none; Node 20.12+)\n\tpython3 -m pip install -q -r quickstart/python/requirements.txt\ntest:            ## run both snippets against the mock: success, 401, 403, 429, 500, 503, missing token\n\t./mock/run_cases.sh\ncheck: deps test\nisolation:       ## Docker isolation probes for Isolated Setup (no real token)\n\t./agent-sandbox/test-isolation.sh\nlive-py:         ## real API, 1 KiB. Needs .env in quickstart/python\n\tcd quickstart/python && python3 quickstart.py\nlive-js:         ## real API, 1 KiB. Needs .env in quickstart/node\n\tcd quickstart/node && node quickstart.mjs\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Run both snippets against the mock for success, 401, 403, 429, 503 (+ missing token). Exit non-zero on any mismatch.\nset -u\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\nexport QRYPT_BASE_URL=\"http://127.0.0.1:18787\"\nfail=0\ncheck() { # lang mode expect_exit expect_text\n  local lang=$1 mode=$2 code=$3 text=$4 out rc\n  MOCK_MODE=$mode python3 mock/server.py 2>/dev/null & pid=$!; sleep 0.6\n  if [ \"$lang\" = py ]; then out=$(cd quickstart/python && python3 quickstart.py 2>&1); rc=$?\n  else out=$(cd quickstart/node && node quickstart.mjs 2>&1); rc=$?; fi\n  kill $pid; wait $pid 2>/dev/null\n  if [ $rc -eq $code ] && grep -q \"$text\" <<<\"$out\"; then echo \"PASS $lang $mode -> exit $rc: $out\"\n  else echo \"FAIL $lang $mode (exit $rc, wanted $code /$text/): $out\"; fail=1; fi\n}\nfor lang in py js; do\n  export QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED]\n  check $lang success 0 \"Success\"\n  check $lang 401 1 \"401\"\n  check $lang 403 1 \"Token invalid OR\"\n  check $lang 429 1 \"wait 10 s or more\"\n  check $lang 503 1 \"Try again shortly\"\n  check $lang 500 1 \"Try again shortly\"\n  check $lang html 1 \"non-JSON reply\"\n  QRYPT_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9 check $lang neterr 1 \"Network error\"\n  QRYPT_API_KEY= check $lang success 1 \"is missing: add to .env. Token: portal.qrypt.com/trial-signup-entropy\"\ndone\nexit $fail\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Trusted live verification. Runs OUTSIDE the agent container.\n# Loads QRYPT_API_KEY from a .env the agent cannot see, then runs FIXED\n# snippets from this repo (never agent-modifiable code) against the live API.\n# Prints only a sanitized success/failure line. Never prints the token, the\n# entropy, or the key.\n#\n# Usage:\n#   agent-sandbox/verify.sh --env ~/.config/qrypt/.env [--lang py|js|both]\n#\n# The --env path MUST NOT be inside a directory the agent container mounts.\nset -euo pipefail\nhere=$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\nrepo=$(cd \"$here/..\" && pwd)\nenvf=\"\"; lang=both; base=\"\"\nwhile [ $# -gt 0 ]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --env) envf=$(realpath \"${2:?}\"); shift 2;;\n    --lang) lang=${2:?}; shift 2;;\n    --base-url) base=${2:?}; shift 2;;\n    *) echo \"usage: verify.sh --env <path> [--lang py|js|both]\" >&2; exit 2;;\n  esac\ndone\n[ -n \"$envf\" ] && [ -f \"$envf\" ] || { echo \"verify.sh: --env <existing-file> is required\" >&2; exit 2; }\n# Optional: point at the mock server (CI / dry-run). Live is the default.\n[ -n \"$base\" ] && export QRYPT_BASE_URL=\"$base\"\n\n# Refuse if the env file is world-readable or owned oddly (mode must be 600/400).\nmode=$(stat -c '%a' \"$envf\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f '%Lp' \"$envf\")\ncase \"$mode\" in 600|400|0400|0600) ;; *)\n  echo \"verify.sh: refusing $envf (mode $mode). chmod 600 it first.\" >&2; exit 2;;\nesac\n\n# Work in a private temp dir the agent never sees. Copy FIXED snippets only.\nwork=$(mktemp -d); trap 'rm -rf \"$work\"' EXIT\nmkdir -p \"$work/py\" \"$work/js\"\ncp \"$repo/quickstart/python/quickstart.py\" \\\n   \"$repo/quickstart/python/requirements.txt\" \"$work/py/\"\ncp \"$repo/quickstart/node/quickstart.mjs\" \"$work/js/\"\n# Place .env next to each snippet WITHOUT printing it.\ncp \"$envf\" \"$work/py/.env\" && chmod 600 \"$work/py/.env\"\ncp \"$envf\" \"$work/js/.env\" && chmod 600 \"$work/js/.env\"\n\nrun_one() {\n  local name=$1; shift\n  local out rc\n  set +e\n  out=$(\"$@\" 2>&1)\n  rc=$?\n  set -e\n  # Scrub anything that looks like a token or long base64 blob from the output\n  # we show the user. Only the success/error line should remain.\n  if [ $rc -eq 0 ] && grep -q '^Success:' <<<\"$out\"; then\n    echo \"verify $name: PASS (AES-GCM round trip; key not shown)\"\n    if [ -z \"$base\" ]; then\n      mkdir -p \"$repo/reports\"\n      echo \"live bytes: 1024 (verify.sh $name $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%MZ))\" >> \"$repo/reports/live-usage.log\"\n    fi\n    return 0\n  fi\n  # Map known friendly errors; never echo raw output (may contain headers).\n  if grep -q 'QRYPT_API_KEY is missing' <<<\"$out\"; then\n    echo \"verify $name: FAIL (missing token in --env file)\"; return 1\n  fi\n  if grep -qE '^40[013]|429|50[03]|Network error' <<<\"$out\"; then\n    echo \"verify $name: FAIL ($(grep -oE '^[0-9]{3}|Network error[^.]+' <<<\"$out\" | head -1))\"\n    return 1\n  fi\n  echo \"verify $name: FAIL (non-zero exit; details suppressed)\"\n  return 1\n}\n\nfail=0\nif [ \"$lang\" = py ] || [ \"$lang\" = both ]; then\n  python3 -m venv \"$work/py/.venv\" >/dev/null\n  \"$work/py/.venv/bin/pip\" -q install -r \"$work/py/requirements.txt\" >/dev/null\n  (cd \"$work/py\" && run_one python .venv/bin/python quickstart.py) || fail=1\nfi\nif [ \"$lang\" = js ] || [ \"$lang\" = both ]; then\n  (cd \"$work/js\" && run_one node node quickstart.mjs) || fail=1\nfi\n# Log bytes used without recording the token (1 KiB per successful call).\nexit $fail\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
